! -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
! Traverse ACROSS the private flux region, to resolve which way the ExB
! circulation runs between the two divertor targets.
!
! Run:  jorek2_postproc < postproc_pfr_line.in
! Then: util/analyse_pfr_line.py pol_line_*.dat
!
! WHY NOT THE BOUNDARY. util/analyse_targets.py measures Phi and n at the
! targets, which is where the sheath sets the potential - but the transfer of
! plasma between the legs happens in the PFR VOLUME. A boundary trace only sees
! where field lines land. Measured on the real run, the ExB direction coherence
! |mean(v)|/mean(|v|) on the inner leg was 0.26 (baseline) and 0.001 (puffed):
! the direction rotates within the averaging window, so the boundary mean
! carries no direction at all. The outer leg was fine (0.97), which is exactly
! the trap - half the answer looks solid.
!
! GEOMETRY - THIS IS THE PART TO GET RIGHT. A flux is an integral through a
! SURFACE, so the cut must be perpendicular to the transfer you want to measure
! and the velocity must be projected on the cut's NORMAL, not its tangent. To
! measure inner <-> outer transfer, the cut is therefore VERTICAL at about the
! X-point major radius - it divides the two divertors - and the normal is R_hat.
! A line drawn from one leg to the other runs PARALLEL to the transfer and its
! flux integral means something else entirely.
!
! The script reports Gamma = 2*pi * int n (v.n_hat) R dl in particles/s, with
! the 2*pi*R factor for the toroidal revolution. Check the printed n_hat and
! psi_N range before trusting the sign.
!
! For AUG 38773 with the strike points at (1.256,-1.055) and (1.593,-1.150),
! and the X-point near (1.43,-0.93):
! -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

namelist input

set units 0          ! SI, as for the target export
set linepoints 400

for step 3800 to 3900 do
  expressions R Z Psi_N Phi T_e T_i ne V_ExB_R V_ExB_Z

  ! DIVIDING CUT: vertical, at the X-point major radius, from the floor up to
  ! just below the X-point. This is the surface that SEPARATES the inner
  ! divertor from the outer, so the flux through it IS the inter-leg transfer.
  ! Its normal is +R_hat, so positive Gamma means inner -> outer.
  pol_line 1.43 -1.16 1.43 -0.94 0.

  ! Secondary: across the PFR, inner leg -> outer leg. Useful for seeing the
  ! potential and density structure, but its normal is roughly vertical, so the
  ! flux through it is NOT the inter-leg transfer - do not read it as such.
  pol_line 1.29 -1.08 1.56 -1.13 0.
done
